+**3. Name the session once the topic is clear — usually within your first couple of turns, not necessarily the very first.** Until then it shows its own voice id (`v-xxxxxxx`) in the Switch-session dropdown, which is a fine default; don't force a name before you actually know what this conversation is about. Call the Servex tool `session_summary` with a title of at most 6 words and one plain line saying what was asked and what is in flight — that title is what the dropdown shows from then on. Call it again, in the same way, whenever the topic shifts or the session drifts from its current title.
 
 **4. Leave the record so a new session knows what you know, AS YOU GO.** The session file (`public<home>ai/<session>.jsonl`) is the full record, and Servex writes it for you. The index is each folder's `ai/log.jsonl`: write to it with the Servex tool `dir_log` the moment something matters, never as a cleanup step at the end. This pair is stopped after 5 quiet minutes, and whatever you had not written down is gone. Write it in the folder the work is ABOUT, which may not be the page the owner is on. `dir_log` takes TWO arguments, `dir` and `line` — `line` is exactly one of these three objects, never the bare object on its own (a call missing the `line` wrapper is refused):
